d and 3 blue bag, keyed red) address this clause.\"}, \"certain\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F01\", \"template\": \"{term}\", \"reasoning\": \"F01 prints the gated word certain as a correct answer or choice, so the clause is producible.\"}, \"impossible\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F03\", \"template\": \"{term}\", \"reasoning\": \"F03 prints the gated word impossible as a correct answer or choice, so the clause is producible.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F06\", \"F07\", \"F11\", \"F12\", \"F14\", \"F15\", \"F16\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Count the favorable outcomes and compare to the total to decide.\", \"{capitalize}: can never happen (probability = 0).\", \"{capitalize}: will always happen (probability = 1).\", \"{answer}\", \"{distractors}\", \"{question}\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"Several bank rows are wrong for the learner. Two rows about picking red or blue (5 red and 5 blue balls, and a two-section red and blue spinner) key equally likely, but picking red or blue is certain, so F14 and F16 print a false statement. A row with a spinner of 3 yellow, 1 red and 1 green sections keys red or green as least likely (F14), while its distractor blue (F15) is the true answer, because blue has no sections and is impossible. F12 repeats these wrong keys, so it is also at fault. F06 uses favorable outcomes, and F07 and F11 use probability = 0 and probability = 1. The word probability and the phrase favorable outcomes are not in cumulative_vocab, introduces_vocab, or any listed vocabulary, and they go beyond the grade 3 quarter 3 gate. The other clauses are producible, but the content is not safe to certify.\"}",
